g, not a quota issue: `local-bin/code-review-runner.sh: line 415: codex_model_args[@]: unbound variable`. This happens in the same `run_llm()` function\'s Codex branch, where `codex_model_args=()` is declared as an empty array and later expanded as `"${codex_model_args[@]}"` - under `set -u`/nounset with an old bash (macOS ships bash 3.2 by default), expanding an empty array this way throws "unbound variable" instead of expanding to nothing. The captain wants this fixed too, in the same pass, since it is the same function and the same class of small robustness bug.\\012\\012After both fixes are merged, the captain wants `docs-ssot-audit` and `doctrine-review` actually re-run today using the new Gemini override set to `gemini-3.8-flash-high`, not the Codex path.\\012\\012## Firstmate spec\\012Read `local-bin/code-review-runner.sh`\'s `run_llm()` function fully before editing, including both `run_gemini_prompt` call sites (the primary auditor path and any adversary/consensus path that also builds `gemini_model`), so the override applies everywhere the Gemini tier is actually invoked, not just one call site.\\012\\0121. Add an environment-variable override for the Gemini model/effort selection, following the exact existing pattern for `CODE_REVIEW_CODEX_MODEL`/`CODEX_MODEL` a few lines above in the same function (env var wins when set, falls back to the current hardcoded `gemini-3.7-flash-${gemini_effort}` derivation when unset). Suggested name: `CODE_REVIEW_GEMINI_MODEL` (full model id like `gemini-3.8-flash-high`, bypassing the `-${gemini_effort}` suffix construction entirely when set, since the override string already names its own effort tier).\\0122. Do not change default behavior when the env var is unset - this is purely additive, same as the existing Codex model override.\\0123. Also fix the Codex branch\'s `codex_model_args[@]: unbound variable` bug in the same function: guard the empty-array expansion so it works under nounset with an old bash (e.g. `"${codex_model_args[@]+"${codex_model_args[@]}"}"` or an equivalent portable guard - check what style the rest of the script already uses for optional array args, if any, and match it). Verify the fix by actually invoking the script with `CODE_REVIEW_CODEX_ONLY=1` and no model override set (the exact case that failed today) and confirming it no longer throws that error, using the real system `/bin/bash` (not an explicitly newer bash) since that mismatch is what caused today\'s failure.\\0124. Keep the diff minimal: this one function\'s model-selection logic for both the Gemini and Codex branches, nothing else in the script.\\0125. Add a small regression test if this repo\'s existing test conventions make that cheap (check for existing tests covering `code-review-runner.sh`\'s tier selection before deciding whether to add one or whether it\'s out of proportion for a one-line override).\\0126. Delivery mode is direct-PR with yolo on (internal automation tooling, per this project\'s registered posture) - push and open the PR yourself, no additional pipeline needed beyond CI green.\\0127. After the PR merges, report back to firstmate with `done:` so firstmate can re-run docs-ssot-audit and doctrine-review with the new override once the fix is on main. Do not run those audits yourself; that is firstmate\'s follow-up, not part of this task\'s definition of done.\\012\\012# Herdr lifecycle declaration - NOT ENABLED\\012**HARD SAFETY GATE:** this scaffold cannot inspect the task text filled in above.\\012If the task will start, stop, delete, restart, profile, or otherwise drive Herdr lifecycle behavior, stop and regenerate the brief with `--herdr-lab` before dispatch.\\012Do not add Herdr lifecycle commands to this unguarded brief by hand.\\012\\012# Setup\\012You are in a disposable git worktree of /Users/irene/Developer/IMAC, at a detached HEAD on a clean default branch.\\012\\012**Verify isolation before anything else.** Run `pwd -P` and `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`; both mus