마라. 검증 방법과 결과를 report.md/PR 설명에 남겨라. 실제 삭제를 실행하기 직전에 `needs-decision`으로 캡틴의 최종 확인을 받아라 — 이건 캡틴의 전역 설정 파일이라 되돌리기 어렵다.\012\012# Herdr lifecycle declaration - NOT ENABLED\012**HARD SAFETY GATE:** this scaffold cannot inspect the task text filled in above.\012If the task will start, stop, delete, restart, profile, or otherwise drive Herdr lifecycle behavior, stop and regenerate the brief with `--herdr-lab` before dispatch.\012Do not add Herdr lifecycle commands to this unguarded brief by hand.\012\012# Setup\012You are in a disposable git worktree of IMAC, at a detached HEAD on a clean default branch.\012\012**Verify isolation before anything else.** Run `pwd -P` and `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`; both must resolve to the disposable task worktree you were launched in, such as a treehouse pool path or an Orca-managed worktree, not the primary checkout firstmate operates from.\012The path check is authoritative: `git rev-parse --git-dir` and `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` can help inspect the repo, but they do not prove you are outside the primary checkout.\012If the top-level path is the primary checkout or not the worktree you were launched in, STOP - do not branch or commit here - append `blocked [at=<epoch>]: launched in primary checkout, not an isolated worktree` to the status file and stop.\012\0121. First action: create your branch: `git checkout -b fm/imac-claude-agents-md-migration-20260924`\012\012# Rules\0121. Never push to the default branch (push only your `fm/imac-claude-agents-md-migration-20260924` branch). Never merge a PR.\0122. Stay inside this worktree; modify nothing outside it.\0123. Use gh-axi for GitHub operations and chrome-devtools-axi for browser operations.\0124. Report status by appending one line:\012   `echo "{state} [at=<epoch>]: {one short line}" >> '\''/Users/irene/Developer/kunchenguid_repos/firstmate/state/imac-claude-agents-md-migration-20260924.status'\''`\012   States: working, needs-decision, blocked, paused, done, failed.\012   Substitute `<epoch>` with the current Unix time in seconds - run `date +%s` and write the number it printed; a stamp that is not plain digits records no time at all.\012   Each append wakes firstmate, so report sparingly: only phase changes a supervisor\012   would act on (setup done, bug reproduced, fix implemented, validation passed) and the\012   needs-decision/blocked/paused/done/failed states. No step-by-step FYI progress lines;\012   firstmate reads your pane for that.\012   Whenever you mention a PR anywhere - a status line, your terminal, a summary - write its full\012   https:// URL exactly as the forge printed it, never a bare number such as "PR 108"; firstmate\012   copies that URL from your line rather than assembling one.\012   A mid-task `working:` line (including setup complete) is nonterminal: do not end the\012   turn after it; continue the same stage until a defined `done:` gate under Definition of done.\012   Use `paused: {why}` - distinct from `blocked:` - ONLY when you are deliberately idling on a\012   known external wait you expect to clear on its own (an upstream release, a rate-limit reset, a scheduled window, or your own validation round):\012   firstmate then leaves your idle pane alone and rechecks it on a long\012   cadence instead of treating it as a possible wedge. Use `blocked:` when you are stuck and need help.\0125. If you hit the same obstacle twice, append `blocked [at=<epoch>]: {why}` and stop; firstmate will help.\0126. If a decision belongs above the implementation worker (product choices, destructive actions),\012   append `needs-decision [at=<epoch>]: {summary of options}` and stop. Firstmate will reply with the decision.\012\012   A decision or blocker you opened stays open until a `resolved` line carrying its exact key lands; a later `done:` or `working:` line never closes it, even when the answer is what started that work.\012   Firstmate'\''s reply normally writes that closing line at answer time; when a blocker or wait clears WITHOUT a firstmate reply, append `resolved [at=<epoch>]: {how it cleared}` yourself (same `[key=<slug>]` if you opened it with one) as you resume.\0127. Never stop, restart, or update the shared `no-mistakes` daemon - it is one instance serving\012   every lane/home, so restarting it kills other lanes'\'' in-flight pipeline runs; only firstmate\012   manages the daemon.\012   Before you append `blocked:` about the pipeline, run `no-mistakes daemon status` and\012   `no-mistakes axi status`. If the daemon socket refuses connections or is missing, append\012   `blocked [at=<epoch>]: {the daemon error}` and stop even when the local run record still says running or\012   fixing, because that record can be stale after the daemon exits. A run record failed with a\012   daemon error is also a real block.\012   Only after ruling out socket refusal, if the run is still running or fixing, reattach and keep\012   going. A drive-call error, timeout, slow read, or generic unreachability is NOT a daemon error:\012   the daemon accepts `respond` immediately and runs the round in the background, so a killed or\012   timed-out call was only waiting for a read while the run kept working.\012\012# Firstmate instruction inbox\012Firstmate steers you through durable message files in '\''/Users/irene/Developer/kunchenguid_repos/firstmate/state/imac-claude-agents-md-migration-20260924.inbox'\''.\012When a terminal message says an instruction is waiting there - and at any natural checkpoint when you are unsure - list '\''/Users/irene/Developer/kunchenguid_repos/firstmate/state/imac-claude-agents-md-migration-20260924.inbox'\''/*.msg, read and act on each message in numeric order, then acknowledge each handled message by moving it: `mv '\''/Users/irene/Developer/kunchenguid_repos/firstmate/state/imac-claude-agents-md-migration-20260924.inbox'\''/NNN.msg '\''/Users/irene/Developer/kunchenguid_repos/firstmate/state/imac-claude-agents-md-migration-20260924.inbox'\''/handled/`.\012The move IS the acknowledgement: without it firstmate rings again and eventually treats you as stuck. An empty or absent inbox needs no action.\012\012# Project memory\012If `AGENTS.md` or `CLAUDE.md` already exists, or if this task produced durable project-intrinsic knowledge, run `/Users/irene/Developer/kunchenguid_repos/firstmate/bin/fm-ensure-agents-md.sh .` in the worktree.\012Record only project knowledge useful to almost every future session.\012For anything the codebase already shows, prefer a pointer to the authoritative file, command, or doc over copying the detail.\012If you touch a project `AGENTS.md`, follow `/Users/irene/Developer/kunchenguid_repos/firstmate/bin/fm-ensure-agents-md.sh`'\''s self-governance contract in the same pass.\012Keep it proportionate: skip `AGENTS.md` edits for trivial tasks that produced no durable project knowledge.\012\012# Definition of done\012Delivery contract: mode=direct-PR\012This task ships **direct-PR**: you raise the PR yourself, without the no-mistakes pipeline.\012The task is complete only when committed on your branch.\012When it is implemented and committed, push your branch and open a PR with `gh-axi`, then append `done [at=<epoch>]: PR {url}` to the status file and stop.\012Do NOT run /no-mistakes. The configured merge authority decides whether to merge the PR; firstmate relays the outcome.\012\012## Progress note (2026-09-24T12:06:18Z)\012\012This task was relaunched. Continue from here; the local copy and every\012uncommitted change are exactly as the previous worker left them.\012\012First, check your instruction inbox: list /Users/irene/Developer/kunchenguid_repos/firstmate/state/imac-claude-agents-md-migration-20260924.inbox/*.msg, act on\012each message in numeric order, then mv each handled file into\012/Users/irene/Developer/kunchenguid_repos/firstmate/state/imac-claude-agents-md-migration-20260924.inbox/handled/. A steer sent before the relaunch survives there.\012\012Verification blocker cleared. Your prio